let dpr=1;
function resize(){ dpr=Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio||1,2); canvas.width=Math.round(W*dpr); canvas.height=Math.round(H*dpr); ctx.setTransform(dpr,0,0,dpr,0,0); baseCache=null; titleCache=null; endingCache=null; }
```
Wait changing canvas.width resets transform. Need setTransform after. render also sets each frame. fine.
- `makeCanvas` imports uses document createElement; create with W*dpr, H*dpr. `makeCanvas(w,h)`.
- buildBase:
```js
function buildBase(sceneId){
 const scene=scenes[sceneId];
 const c=makeCanvas(Math.round(W*dpr),Math.round(H*dpr));
 const g=c.getContext('2d');
 g.scale(dpr,dpr);
 scene.draw(g,state);
 baseCache=c; baseScene=sceneId;
}
```
If scene.draw uses `ctx.canvas.width` e.g. drawTitle not; scene draw doesn't. Good.
- `renderGame` if baseScene !== currentScene build. For postgame ending shop, base unchanged. fine.
- Title base with drawTitleBase; cache at dpr. Ending base.
- Need `ctx.imageSmoothingEnabled = true`.

Player variable:
```js
const player={x:640,y:548,dir:'up',walk:0,moving:false,step:0};
function syncPlayerFromState(){...}
```
state.player stored. On load.

`currentScene` initial 'shop'; `mode='title'`, endingKey=null.

Movement:
```js
const keys=new Set();
function moveInput() { ... }
```
`touchVector`.

Update:
```js
function update(dt) {
 if (mode==='game') {
   state.playtime += dt;
   if (!canControl()) { player.moving=false; return; }
   ...
 }
}
```
`canControl` = !ui.isBlocking() && !transitioning && !storyBusy.

When blocked, clear keys? Movement keys remain pressed; on resume may move instantly. Fine, but if overlay open and key up happens, keys state handled. Could clear on overlay open? Not necessary.
- If state.flags.finished? Allow movement postgame.

Auto-walk pending:
```js
let moveTarget=null, pendingHotspot=null;
function moveToward(target,dt){
 const dx=target.x-player.x, dy=target.y-player.y;
 if (hypot<6) return false;
 const step=150*dt; if(step>=dist){ player.x=target.x; player.y=target.y;} else...
 return {dx,dy};
}
```
Collision: We can't just set target if unwalkable; target chosen walkable. Axis collision.
- Simpler vector + tryMove. If both blocked, no.
```js
function tryMove(dx,dy) {
 const dist=hypot...
 const nx=player.x+dx*..., ny=...
 if (isWalkable(currentScene,nx,player.y,12)) player.x=nx;
 if (isWalkable(currentScene,player.x,ny,12)) player.y=ny;
}
```
- For keyboard normalized. `dx,dy` unit.
- Walk animation phase increment when actually moved. Use before/after positions.
- Step sound: accumulate stepDist; when >34 -> sound.step(outdoor), reset. Or timer. Add `stepAccum += movedDist`. Outdoor bool.
- Dir based on dx/dy.

When reached target:
```js
if (moveTarget && dist<7) { moveTarget=null; if(pendingHotspot){ const h=pendingHotspot; pendingHotspot=null; if(nearHotspot(h)) interactHotspot(h);} }
```
- If user presses movement keys, moveTarget=null; pendingHotspot=null.

Interaction:
```js
let interacting=false;
async function interactHotspot(h){
 if(!h||interacting||ui.isBlocking()||mode!=='game') return;
 interacting=true;
 ui.setPrompt(null); currentPrompt=null;
 sound.click();
 try { await handleAction(h.action,h); } catch(err) { console.error(err); await ui.say([{who:null,text:'The evening stutters. Something small has gone missing.'}]); }
 interacting=false;
 saveState();
 ui.refreshHUD();
}
```
- After go scene, currentScene changes; prompt update next frame.
- If handleAction opens inspect, await resolves on close. good.
- If handleAction opens evidence, returns immediately (not await close) because story handleAction `ui.openEvidence(...)` returns. `interacting=false` while evidence open; interactions blocked by ui.isBlocking. fine.
- For station desk story polls evidence close, so awaited. good.

`nearestHotspot()`:
```js
let best=null,bd=1e9;
for h of hotspotsAt(currentScene,state){ const d=hypot(h.x-player.x,h.y-player.y); if(d < h.r+30 && d<bd){...}}
return best;
```
Potential overlap in tea fixed.
- Use player feet.

Click:
```js
function canvasPoint(e){...}
function hotspotAt(x,y){ for h... if dist < Math.max(h.r*0.85,32) ...}
```
If click exactly on player no.
- On pointerdown only primary; ignore if ui blocking; if e.button!==0.
- If hotspot found and near: interact immediately. Else target approach.
- If no hotspot: target nearestWalkable(clicked) with radius 12; set pending null.
- Also if click within e.g. 20 of player, no.

Approach for far hotspot:
```js
const p=approachPoint(currentScene,player,h);
if(p){moveTarget=p;pendingHotspot=h;} else if(dist < h.r+80){interactHotspot(h);}
```
- If p equals player? still. Fine.

`updatePrompt()` every frame:
- if mode!='game'||ui.isBlocking()||transitioning||storyBusy||interacting -> hide.
- nearest. Show label. Maybe if pending target show "Walking to..."? no.
- stage-inner clickable based on hotspot hover from pointermove only. We'll set in pointermove.

Pointermove:
```js
if(mode!=='game'||ui.isBlocking()) return;
const p=canvasPoint(e); const h=hitHotspot(p.x,p.y);
stageInner.classList.toggle('clickable',!!h);
```

Touch:
- joystick elements check.
- On pointerdown joystick use setPointerCapture? The joystick is div. Add.
- radius = rect.width/2 - 18.
- pointermove on window if id.
- knob style transform `translate(${dx}px,${dy}px)`.
- Store normalized vector (dx/radius,dy/radius) clamped.
- On pointerup reset with transition maybe. CSS knob transition.
- Touch use.

Title/new game:
```js
async function newGame(){
  sound.init(); sound.resume();
  ui.hideTitleInstant();
  resetState();
  state.started = true;
  state.scene='shop';
  state.settings = {...state.settings};
  mode='game'; currentScene='shop'; storyBusy=true;
  endingKey=null; baseCache=null; moveTarget=null; pending=null;
  player x/y from scenes.shop.spawn (640,610) but state play? set.
  state.player=...
  state.visited.shop=true;
  ui.showHUD();
  ui.setPlace(...);
  ui.resetObjectiveTracking();
  sound.setMuted(state.settings.muted);
  sound.setScene('shop');
  buildBase? render next frame.
  await ui.fadeOut(0)? No curtain covers. `ui.curtain` starts after. There may be a flash of shop before curtain appears? startIntro calls ui.curtain immediately (synchronous first line) after awaited? StartIntro is async and called; `await startIntro()` begins executing immediately until first await; it calls `await ui.curtain(...)`, which sets curtain visible synchronously then awaits. So curtain appears before next paint. Good.
  await startIntro();
  storyBusy=false;
  ui.refreshHUD();
}
```
- resetState keeps settings and saves; state.started false. We set true.
- `state.flags.introDone` set in story. fine.
- Watch flag set in story.
- Need state.started true in story before. yes.
- `ui.hideTitleInstant` hides title. Great.
- `ui.fadeIn` not needed.
- If startIntro throws, catch.

- `continueGame`:
```js
sound.init(); sound.resume(); ui.hideTitleInstant();
const loaded=loadState();
if(!loaded){ return newGame(); }
syncFromSave();
mode='game'; currentScene=state.scene && scenes[state.scene]?state.scene:'shop';
baseCache=null; sync player; storyBusy=true;
ui.showHUD; setPlace; resetObjective; apply settings; sound mute/scene;
await ui.fadeOut(0); maybe no, title hidden -> canvas shows scene immediately. use ui.fadeIn(800) (fade starts transparent, no black). Could `ui.fadeOut(250);` then hide title etc then fadeIn. Title hide is instant; a fade black would mask pop. Sequence:
  1. ui.hideTitleInstant
  2. ui.fadeOut(50)? fade black but CSS transition .55 and waiting 50 means partial.
Better use curtain? For continue, show fade black immediately by adding class then wait 550? That adds delay. Could hide title with `.out` transition (1s) then switch after? Simpler:
  - `ui.fadeOut(0)` adds black instantly? CSS transitions, not instant. Could set style.transition='none' then class black then force, then restore. Not worth. Title fade out 1s: keep title overlay, start fade, etc.
```
async function continueGame(){
 sound.init(); sound.resume();
 const loaded=loadState(); ...
 ui.hideTitle(); // 1s fade
 await wait(350);
 const loaded = loadState(); ...
 // mode switch while title still fading; canvas behind
 ...
 await wait(700) until title hidden
}
```
But loading state after delay. Fine. Yet title screen has opaque gradient; fading reveals scene. Good.
- We can use `ui.fadeOut(500)` first to black while title visible, then hide title instant, switch, fadeIn(900). This is clean:
```js
await ui.fadeOut(500);
ui.hideTitleInstant();
...
await ui.fadeIn(900);
```
Black overlay z52 above title z30, so fades to black. Good. New game could use black fade too, but curtain covers. For new game, hide title instantly and curtain. No fade needed.
- For continue, use fade.

- After continue and mode game, if state.flags.finished maybe objective post. `ui.refreshHUD` with reset no announce. Show location card.
- Call `story.onSceneEnter(currentScene,null)` after `storyBusy=false`? If lighthouse and metJune false, onSceneEnter awaits dialogue. Don't await in continue, call after setting storyBusy false. It will block movement via dialogue. Good.
- If loaded scene has finished and ending, maybe show toast.

- `applySettings`: sound.setMuted; `state.settings.muted`. UI labels update only in pause open; fine.
- `ui.initUI` called at startup before load; state.settings default. On continue, settings labels update when pause opened. fine.

Save/title:
```js
