Alternative: split foreground layer by depth: the foreground furniture fronts at y476..504 should be drawn after entities with y < 476-ish and before entities with y > 476. We can draw scene base, then foreground, then entities sorted; but NPC behind counter y476 (Alma feet) should be before foreground. Need to draw each entity and then overlay foreground if its y < foreground threshold. We can integrate foreground into the sorted entity order:
- Draw base.
- Add a "foreground" pseudo-entity with y = threshold (e.g., 504 or 476). Sort entities by y. Draw each entity; when reaching foreground pseudo-entity, draw scene.drawForeground. This gives correct occlusion:
  - Player y520 > threshold 476 => drawn after foreground -> not covered.
  - Alma y476 is equal; if before foreground? sort with tie; set foreground y=478 maybe, Alma 476 before => covered. Good.
  - Player behind counter y400 < threshold => drawn before foreground -> covered.
